    "chunk_size_bytes": 2003,
    "chunk_text": "No. of benefi-ciaries whose selection decision was changed following the Appeal and Objection Process\n\nUnselected 29,103 20,693 8,410\n\nExtremely Poor\n\n1,763 1,602 161\n\nPoor 4,238 3,400 838\n\nVulnerable 2,688 1,714 974\n\nTransitional 11,939 5,943 5,996\n\nTotal 49,731 33,352 16,379\n\n(v) Such instances have not yet been identified,\n\nand the number of such instances can be accurately determined following an audit investigation to be conducted after completion of the information updating process.\n\n(vi) Pursuant to the recommendation of the\n\nParliamentary Committee made at its Meeting held on November 12, 2025, an Expert Committee comprising the following five members was appointed: Professor Lakshman Dissanayake (Chairman), Professor Seetha Bandara (Member), Dr. Herath Gunathilaka (Member) and Dr. Pulasthi Amarasinghe (Member).\n\nThe Committee reviewed the existing model and weighted criteria and proposed a revised methodology called Vulnerability-Based Targeting and Recertification System (VTRS). After extensive deliberations with the Department of Census and Statistics, the Department of National Planning and the World Bank, views and proposals were obtained. Accordingly, it had been decided to ascertain the appropriateness of this methodology by conducting a pilot study and approval of the Secretary to the Ministry of Finance was sought on June 09, 2026 to proceed with conducting the pilot study. Thus, it was decided to initiate a pilot test with the concurrence and assistance of the Department of Census and Statistics and upon the decision of it, further action will be determined. After the pilot study, it is expected to verify the criteria, the marks awarding procedure, operational definitions, practical use at the field level, data collection process and errors of inclusion and exclusion. Thereafter, the most appropriate methodology for selection and re-verification of beneficiaries in the future will be determined and reported to Parliament.\n\n(b) Not relevant.\n\n1195 1196"
