    "chunk_size_bytes": 2086,
    "chunk_text": "1. What are the monthly and cumulative additional costs on petroleum, gas, coal, fertilizer, freight, insurance and aviation against the pre-war baseline? Separate price, volume and exchange rate effects, public and private costs, avoiding double counting.\n\n\u0dba\u0dd0\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dd9 \u0dbb\u0d94\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dd9\u0ddd\u0db4 \u0dbb \u0dd0 \u0dbb\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dd9 ,\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dd9 \u0dbb\u0db1\u0dd0\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0dbb \u0dd0 \u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0db1\u0db1\u0dd9 \u0dbb \u0dbb\u0db6\u0dd0\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dba\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dca \u0dbb\u0d89\u0dca \u0db1\u0dcf\u0daf.\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd4\u0dba\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dd9\u0db1\u0ddd\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dbb\u0d85 \u0daf\u0dc0\u0dba\u0dbb\u0d9c\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0d85\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dca\u200d\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dbb \u0dc0\u0daf\u0dad\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dd9 \u0dcf\u0daf\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dba\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dca \u0dbb\u0d89\u0dca \u0db1\u0dcf\u0daf.\n\n3. How are these costs financed through revenue, expenditure reductions, borrowing, supplier credit, assistance or reserves? Who ultimately pays? What funds the diesel subsidy ceilings of Rs. 15 billion in October, 2026, Rs.13.5 billion in November, 2026 and Rs. 12.15 billion in December, 2026? What replaces this relief thereafter?\n\nSir, we have been mentioning in this House that if you all want to give a subsidy, ensure that you give it to the CPC and not to the foreign companies. Now, I am happy to see the Hon. Minister Anura Karunathilaka also saying the same thing. So, ensure that these are put to use; you can use that Rs. 40 billion for the people of this country.\n\n4. With September, 2026 gross reserves reported at US Dollars 6.851 billion, what are the usable reserves, restricted swaps, reserve liabilities, IMF net international reserves, import cover and external payments due within twelve months? Distinguish conflict pressures from scheduled repayments and valuation changes.\n\n5. What measureable gains have arisen from diverted shipping, bunkering, aviation, tourism or relocated investment? What is their net foreign exchange contribution after costs?\n\n6. What assumptions underpin the Government\u2019s assessment of the conflict\u2019s remaining duration? Will you table three, six and twelve-month scenarios, covering oil prices, financing gaps, reserves, debt service and contingency triggers?"
  },
  {
