    "chunk_size_bytes": 2082,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf 2\u0dba) \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0da2\u0dba\u0dca\u0dad \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b85\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4) (The Hon. (Dr.) Anil Jayantha) Hon. Member, thank you very much for the comments. Whatever points that you just highlighted could be considered in decision-making, wherever relevant and appropriate.\n\nThen, apart from the development in the Current Account, we have other plans, as you also highlighted, such as promoting foreign direct investments. Of course, there are some threats at this particular moment especially due to the crisis situation in the Middle East. Investors also would take time because they are a little bit sceptical about this situation. But from our side, we are actually taking measures to create a level playing field and a conducive environment, implementing the digitalization process to facilitate them. There are constraints, but we are overcoming all those one by one.\n\nWhen it comes to strengthening the currency, as of now, the actual exchange rate really goes along with the theoretical base. For example, the rupee interest rate is greater than the dollar interest rate. As a result, there is a gradual depreciation of the rupee, it is accepted. It is around 5 to 6 per cent. If it goes beyond that level, then, we need to be a little bit alarmed. So, as of now, the situation is under control. And, the Central Bank and the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development would, from time to time, take decisions pertaining to the stability of the financial sector without leaking information to the interested parties.\n\nThen, if we take the situation at the Colombo Stock Exchange, of course, from time to time, temporary fluctuations could be seen happening. Due to that particular situation, interest rates change. However, we\n\ncan observe that there is no such volatility in the Colombo Stock Exchange. Specially due to the war situation, some declines could be seen, but over time, it would recover and I can assure you that there is no volatility in the Colombo Stock Market."
