    "chunk_text": "\u2022 \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bc1\u0bb1\u0bc8 - \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b87\u0ba3\u0bc8\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 06*\u0bc8\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 06*\u0b87\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb0\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. (\u0b9a\u0bbf\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3 \u0b87\u0ba3\u0bc8\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 06\u0b90\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bc8\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 06\u0b90\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd)\n\n(\u0b88) \u0baa\u0bca\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bc1. \u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bc1.\n\n(a) (i) The targeted number of persons to be directed for foreign employment for the year 2026 is 250,000.\n\n(ii) According to the computer system of the\n\n(iii) Measures are being taken to conduct employment promotion programmes locally and overseas, in accordance with the 2026 Action Plan.\n\nIn order to achieve the above targets, arrangements are being made to conduct employment promotion programmes at national and district levels. Accordingly, the Marketing Division of the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment has planned to conduct nine national-level employment promotion programmes, covering all nine provinces of Sri Lanka. So far, six national-level employment promotion programmes have been conducted covering the Southern, Western, Sabaragamuwa, Uva, North Central and North-Western Provinces.\n\nFurther, arrangements have already been made to conduct foreign employment promotion programmes in the Northern, Central and Eastern Provinces during this year.\n\nIn addition, vocational training guidance programmes covering the entire Island are being conducted by the Marketing Division. So far, 87 such programmes have been conducted through the provincial offices of the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment and arrangements have been made to conduct a further 123 programmes.\n\nFurthermore, two foreign employment promotion programmes have been conducted in South Korea and Japan during 2026 and arrangements are being made to conduct one more foreign employment promotion programme during this year.\n\nIn addition, discussions were held with foreign missions regarding securing foreign employment opportunities for the Sri Lankan community and enhancing their skills, and the necessary arrangements are being made."
