    "chunk_text": "\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bb2\u0bb5\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0baf\u0bae\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bb5\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0baf\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b92\u0ba4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3 \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b92\u0ba4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc0\u0b9f\u0bc1\n\n(\u0bb0\u0bc2\u0baa\u0bbe\u0baf\u0bcd)\n\n\u0b9a\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb3\u0bae\u0bcd 22,500,000,000.00\n\n\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0bbe\u0b95 \u0ba8\u0b9f\u0bb5\u0b9f\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd 680,800,000.00\n\n\u0bb5\u0bb2\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0bc2\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0b9f\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb5\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bbf 500,000,000.00\n\n\u0bb5\u0bb2\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0bc2\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bb2\u0bcd 3,700,000,000.00\n\n2026 \u0db1\u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 04\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 04\n\n(\u0b86) \u0b8f\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0b9f\u0bc8\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2.\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb2.\n\n(a) (i) Yes.\n\n(ii) The Aswesuma beneficiaries empowered\n\nby the Department of Samurdhi Development and other implemented projects are continuously subjected to monitoring and follow up through department officials and an organizational network operated to facilitate this process from the rural level to the national level as follows:\n\nIn addition, information regarding beneficiaries and projects is entered into the EIS system, through which ongoing data-based monitoring is conducted. Furthermore, progress related to this is also discussed at the monthly progress review meetings. held for all district Samudhi Directors, under the chairmanship of the Director General of the Department of Samurdhi Development.\n\n(iii)\n\n(iv) It is planned to use the following economic, educational, health and social indicators to identify an empowered family as a family that has been lifted out of poverty.\n\nEconomic Indicators\n\n\u2022 The monthly individual income of a beneficiary increasing to at least Rs. 40,000.\n\n\u2022 Achieving a minimum annual increase of 10 per cent in individual savings.\n\nEducational Indicators\n\n\u2022 Increase in the number of years children attend to school.\n\n\u2022 Increase in the number of children from Aswesuma families pursuing higher education.\n\n\u2022 Increase in number of children with multi -language capabilities.\n\nHealth Indicators\n\n\u2022 Low level of child malnutrition within\n\nthe family - proper weight for age, proper weight for height, proper height for age.\n\n\u2022 Low percentage of child mortality rate\n\nfor children under five years.\n\n\u2022 Reduction in chronic diseases within the\n\nfamily.\n\n\u2022 Reduction of drug addiction and cigarette\n\nuse within families\n\nSocial Indicators"
  },
